From 9ba1259881bb4fac9072099ef96e7404e0b3bed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:31:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(3d): a non-centre-cutting pass restart over a cleared
 core plunges, not refuses

#3857 applied the full-disc test to each tool at a 3D Pocket pass
restart. For a tool that is not centre-cutting, a restart over a cleared
core then went to the M11.3 fallback, which refuses the operation when
no helix or ramp fits. The core law permits that plunge.

Now the core law decides if a refusal is possible. Over a cleared core
the fallback runs on a copy; a clean helix or ramp is kept, else the
restart plunges by name. Over an uncut core the old refusal stands.

Fixes #3885

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
